{"title":"2025 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_20\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 20</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:40)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:40)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Quick_and_Simple)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Quick and Simple)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_OmegaLearn.org\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by OmegaLearn.org</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_(Fast_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 (Fast and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4_by_MadMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 4 by MadMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_20\">Problem 20</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 20\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Four congruent semicircles are inscribed in a square of side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> so that their diameters are on the sides of the square, one endpoint of each diameter is at a vertex of the square, and adjacent semicircles are tangent to each other. A small circle centered at the center of the square is tangent to each of the four semicircles, as shown below.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/9/999d7699134dfd106175595beed0f608becea47c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import geometry; size(6cm);  real r = (sqrt(3)-1)/2, R = (sqrt(2) - 1)*(sqrt(3)-1)/2; draw((0,0) -- (1,0) -- (1, 1) -- (0,1) -- cycle); draw(arc((r, 0), r, 0, 180)); draw(arc((1, r), r, 90, 270)); draw(arc((1 - r, 1), r, 180, 360)); draw(arc((0, 1 - r), r, 270, 450)); draw(circle((1/2,1/2),R)); [/asy]\" width=\"285\" height=\"285\" />\nThe diameter of the small circle can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/0/1b0763b79c644d95c401e81021ea978cf8f8efb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sqrt a+b)(\\sqrt c+d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"22\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are integers. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/4/e947add5766b9f26f6dfe73d9425d87664416459.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c+d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/5/2e5a87370eeaf8f3e4bff8cbe6564f29ff3f7e22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 3 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 5 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 8 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 9 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"364\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the radius of the large semicircles be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and let the diameter of the inner be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Draw lines as follows:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a0cb2a0a7ba4fc9fad9232c5c27b536c314cdaa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import geometry; size(6cm);  real r = (sqrt(3)-1)/2, R = (sqrt(2) - 1)*(sqrt(3)-1)/2; draw((0,0) -- (1,0) -- (1, 1) -- (0,1) -- cycle); draw(arc((r, 0), r, 0, 180)); draw(arc((1, r), r, 90, 270)); draw(arc((1 - r, 1), r, 180, 360)); draw(arc((0, 1 - r), r, 270, 450)); draw(circle((1/2,1/2),R)); draw((0.36602540378,0)--(0, 0.63397459622),dashed); label(“$r$”,(0,0.45),W); label(“$1-2r$”,(0,0.15),W); label(“$r$”,(0.15,0),S); label(“$r$”,(0.1,0.45),NE); label(“$r$”,(0.275,0.15),NE); label(“$r$”,(0.4,0.15),E); label(“$r$”,(0.6,0.85),E); label(“$D$”,(0.485,0.5),E); draw((0.36602540378,0)--(0.63397459622,1),dashed); label(“$r$”,(0.45,1),N); label(“$1-2r$”,(0.15,1),N); [/asy]\" width=\"285\" height=\"262\" />\nBy the Pythagorean Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/d/64d34e0cc0dcf61c7a9f065deda26a53b9fa2f14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2+(1-r)^2=(2r)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/6/e76f98039b312e3eb0c67bb62f5cbc02a3ffe07c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2r^2+2r-1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/3/cf334bce6c030e49b9d2f963976015fede694472.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"43\" /> (we take the positive solution).\n</p><p>Now apply the Pythagorean Theorem on the quadrilateral’s altitude down to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/3/0d3d971170ae58d8d91a615892a13cb409abb9ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1-2r)^2+1=(2r+D)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"205\" height=\"21\" />. Solving yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e081698e7d585fae95a5e572498ed1d34193e7da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2r+D=\\sqrt{8-4\\sqrt{3}}=\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"259\" height=\"35\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/c/cdc4bd27194c50579025783381494e33fe63a1a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{3}+1=(\\sqrt{3}-1)(\\sqrt{2}-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"354\" height=\"24\" />. Hence the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/9/54926f9d43d1a2114c50131a65372db789380691.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3-1+2-1=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"185\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~ <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Eevee9406\">eevee9406</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have the diagram: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/8/2986b53eaa2707c115ecbf5cf0b5999abfd4f01c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import geometry; size(6cm);  real r = (sqrt(3)-1)/2, R = (sqrt(2) - 1)*(sqrt(3)-1)/2; draw((0,0) -- (1,0) -- (1, 1) -- (0,1) -- cycle); draw(arc((r, 0), r, 0, 180)); draw(arc((1, r), r, 90, 270)); draw(arc((1 - r, 1), r, 180, 360)); draw(arc((0, 1 - r), r, 270, 450)); draw(circle((1/2,1/2),R)); draw((0.36602540378,0)--(0, 0.63397459622),dashed); draw((0.63397459622,1)--(0, 0.63397459622),dashed); draw((0.63397459622,1)--(1, 0.36602540378),dashed); draw((0.36602540378,0)--(1, 0.36602540378),dashed); label(“$x$”,(0.15,0),S); label(“$x$”,(0.1,0.45),SW); label(“$x$”,(0.275,0.15),SW); label(“$x$”,(0.22,0.64)); label(“$r$”,(0.45,0.55)); draw((0.5,0.5)--(0, 0.63397459622),dashed); draw((0.36602540378,0)--(0.5,0.5),dashed); draw((0.18301270189,0.31698729811)--(0.5,0.5),dashed); label(&quot;$J$&quot;,(0.20301270189,0.29698729811),SW); label(“$O$”,(0.485,0.5),E); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0,1),NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(1,1),NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,(0,0),SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(1,0),SE); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,(0.36602540378,0),S); label(&quot;$H$&quot;,(0, 0.63397459622),W); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,(0.63397459622,1),N); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,(1, 0.36602540378),E);  label(“$\\sqrt3 x$”,(0,0.3),W); [/asy]\" width=\"285\" height=\"258\" />\n</p><p>We label the vertices of the square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, the centers of the semicircle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, and the center of the small circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Lets call the radius of the big semicircle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and the radius of the small circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. \n</p><p>Looking at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/f/cdfaaced619d7a7fb36a68999d59e7a17cf46f31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle HDG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />, we can see it is a right triangle as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a square, and we can also observe that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/f/eaf9409044fef7f3966027eec40b2cced52eb16c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DG$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and the hypotenuse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a7a248cfd02095e2a009f811d5732a9bea9d595.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> is exactly twice at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/f/cdfaaced619d7a7fb36a68999d59e7a17cf46f31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle HDG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/7/66759d2a9d96e4673871ea55a6cfa0fd9ec8bfcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-60-90^\\circ$\" width=\"105\" height=\"13\" /> triangle. That means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b83ea2b2676b83c9afe2618c57a9c107b0e1d19d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HD$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/f/0ff2986bb5aa6eabf3095fff97b571e485126fa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt3 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"36\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Upon inspection, we can also see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/3/bb3ddf9a5fa2fca5c4787d4f989af0eef1387bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a unit square with all sides equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we can set the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/6/d96da3b91cd134a225daa1be4aaba212cad06084.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HD+AH=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"120\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/3/513fbb0239ec10b7101ce3547eca2a7d3864bf16.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x+\\sqrt3 x = 1\\]\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />, so solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/4/7a4b06523abddba4196d4b25cbad536fc6aed331.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}\\]\" width=\"92\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Then, if we compose an auxiliary line from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/b/68bc6f8caca948dca03f953aee8ce093afad4d88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, we can observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/5/da577d9057861f002965c78173e2a870fd1004aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle HOJ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is an isosceles right triangle. That means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/3/d638be81dccd4ee8a277a5855132c1ac7c17c55b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+r=\\sqrt2 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"21\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/3/74363485610f0af8fcff5fd4dab9ad8a0091856a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-1-\\sqrt2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"21\" /> relations), which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/0/04025611eadb2796071a2cda7d834edbcf67bde8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r=(\\sqrt2 -1)x\\]\" width=\"112\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>We're asked to find the diameter of the small circle, so we can multiply the equation by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfc499803e45fb0e66024d70690152c58471d763.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2r=2(\\sqrt2 -1)x\\]\" width=\"130\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Plugging x in, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> multiplied and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the denominator cancel out, and we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/5/8d5dacd0ec247727d0469527b262bf95ae0872d7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2r=2(\\sqrt2 -1)(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2})\\]\" width=\"192\" height=\"41\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/3/aa3e662cd8af2c18246d255eb7f1ef1e1903e637.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2r=(\\sqrt2 -1)(\\sqrt3 -1)\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> respectively, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e084da61f7fdc8edcf0b60f5093f387bcfd7f009.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+(-1)+3+(-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" /> gets us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/2/612dd005061b65928c17969e4e11f44e6c62a746.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>-Neo\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the centers of the four circles on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc143c3f887fa7e92fd80d91bb22af51b4abd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> be equal to the radius of one of the semicircles and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4f3f4b698ce35667432041e168f7653533fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> be the radius of the inner circle. From the diagram from solution 2, we can easily recognize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/4/a3496242cb32237134d9d790f77ec6b1eb792027.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DHG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c78b85058ee5e17f88e2cde302e48aad826b35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-60-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> triangle. We now form an equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/8/408dacb71eeeb70497b0a67d79a5193d8be57dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1 + r_1\\sqrt{3} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"22\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc143c3f887fa7e92fd80d91bb22af51b4abd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> we will get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/7/06777b50eeae12f7ad3f9b79c692ae2fa4da731b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"43\" /> as the radius. We now need to recognize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/3/9735b37ac43861ef9e105bff1711f117917b09ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EFGH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> is a square. We can also see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f3f219818f8d0eac8eef20c351b675279b48e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HF = 2r_1+2r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"17\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/3/9735b37ac43861ef9e105bff1711f117917b09ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EFGH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> is a square, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/8/d18f5bb2c178cb92d3aaa1b03b632fa5fd0f1aad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HG = 2r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"17\" />, we can figure out that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/2/b6296724bd673c059969a2b5002cf211a03e62cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HF = 2r_1\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"22\" />. The final step is to plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc143c3f887fa7e92fd80d91bb22af51b4abd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> and solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/1/531a17678c4a3f050fe115e5a12d9bc3c4e5ca83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" /> (not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4f3f4b698ce35667432041e168f7653533fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> as the question asks for the diameter).\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/3/5738763eba618128117908e2b7f0fd0e30259bad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2})\\sqrt{2} = 2(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}) + 2r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"263\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/b/f5b3ab135e635889c681bc5ba35faa7769fceaa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sqrt{3}-1)\\sqrt{2} = \\sqrt{3}-1 + 2r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"223\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/6/0d60e8a45eb339d4ae22290d69d73a4de361a761.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sqrt{3}-1)(\\sqrt{2}-1) = 2r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"190\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/7/557e6acf61edd17a7fe724a914b764f081a98544.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 - 1 + 2 - 1 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"179\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~ROGER8432V3\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We realize that we can connect the radii of the semicircles to form an inner square (let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> denote the radius of the semicircles and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> denote their diameter)\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/f/a5f8eced7833f891c90543b0b9f60867e0848cfe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import geometry; size(6cm);  real r = (sqrt(3)-1)/2, R = (sqrt(2) - 1)*(sqrt(3)-1)/2; draw((0,0) -- (1,0) -- (1, 1) -- (0,1) -- cycle); draw((1,0.366025403784) -- (0.366025403784, 0)); draw((0.366025403784, 0) -- (0, 0.63397459621)); draw((1,0.366025403784) -- (0.63397459621, 1)); draw((0.63397459621, 1) -- (0, 0.63397459621)); draw(arc((r, 0), r, 0, 180)); draw(arc((1, r), r, 90, 270)); draw(arc((1 - r, 1), r, 180, 360)); draw(arc((0, 1 - r), r, 270, 450)); draw(circle((1/2,1/2),R)); draw(brace((0,0), (0, 0.63397459621)), black+0.4bp); draw(brace((0.366025403784), (0,0)), black+0.4bp); label(&quot;$1-r$&quot;, (-0.2, 0.3169872981)); label(&quot;$r$&quot;, (0.8, 0.28)); label(&quot;$r$&quot;, (0.18301270189, -0.08)); label(&quot;$r$&quot;, (0.55, 0.139)); [/asy]\" width=\"285\" height=\"242\" />\nTo find the length of the inner square, we apply the Pythagorean Theorem\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/5/3853347563ec69bdf540d0047f9f8448e81bab47.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(1 - r)^{2}+r^{2}= (2r)^{2}\\]\" width=\"160\" height=\"20\" />\nWe now substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/9/fa974f81e42cef14451b5d1aa0857c7b20d8924a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{d}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/0/89003b465f2312ce7bea834b46c6bb36a1764c83.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(1 - \\frac{d}{2})^2+(\\frac{d}{2})^{2}= d^{2}\\]\" width=\"162\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/c/72c69777bb01ed02421b736db744f908d78b4321.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1-d + \\frac{d^2}{4}+\\frac{d^{2}}{4}= d^{2}\\]\" width=\"165\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/b/9abbfe8ed164c3a62b37f672500ef8263a33b1bd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{d^{2}}{2} -d+1= d^{2}\\]\" width=\"121\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/1/d714134c63ec0faed6886d3941fecd06b8b22bd3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d^{2} -2d+2= 2d^{2}\\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/7/bf71e6dfe6cb3efd7dabf54dce367edcb6d5a620.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-d^{2} -2d+2= 0\\]\" width=\"134\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/4/8e485948cc254427e439499d19a5d2742d25167f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d^{2} +2d-2= 0\\]\" width=\"121\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/1/e412ffff39742a97166a5ba050a2a5027ac93c04.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^{2}-4ac}}{2a}\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"40\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/3/f73723ae7d71786638c25bda11ae3b728f00da14.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d = \\frac{-2 \\pm \\sqrt{4-4(-2)}}{2}\\]\" width=\"176\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/1/721f085d46b396995446f268b7bd2bfeb95a47e0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d = \\frac{-2 \\pm \\sqrt{12}}{2}\\]\" width=\"114\" height=\"41\" />\nWe must only consider the positive solution\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/9/8291be4f7be52439496757c096190a942d9cb85b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d = \\frac{-2 + \\sqrt{12}}{2}\\]\" width=\"114\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7c214317fccc05e32c8e5c6be73bb14ff97af5c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d = \\frac{-2 + 2\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\]\" width=\"114\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/b/24bf3e2cd6b6fa20420c40c15facbabea2f0f661.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d = -1 + \\sqrt{3}\\]\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/7/797aa03d2cc5ee734c300eaacefae68b17d9f8ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d = \\sqrt{3} -1\\]\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" />\nThe diagonal of the inner square measures <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb3b22896ebc8528e7c366af15278151a393bffb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"36\" height=\"21\" />.\nIt can also be represented as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/5/5257c2bc7f375eb0fdee37befeb5d10be4927ecd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d+ d_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/6/44612d9d6ec37da7f4edd0f205d65cdac5954dc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> denotes small circle's diameter. I demonstrate this below\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/b/68be4fb8d2a43f67d0c77ed370c0ac75ebc670e3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import geometry; size(6cm); real r = (sqrt(3)-1)/2, R = (sqrt(2) - 1)*(sqrt(3)-1)/2; draw((0,0) -- (1,0) -- (1, 1) -- (0,1) -- cycle); draw((1,0.366025403784) -- (0.366025403784, 0)); draw((0.366025403784, 0) -- (0, 0.63397459621)); draw((1,0.366025403784) -- (0.63397459621, 1)); draw((0.63397459621, 1) -- (0, 0.63397459621)); draw((1,0.366025403784) -- (0, 0.63397459621)); draw(brace((1,0.366025403784), (0.649, 0.456)), black+0.4bp); draw(brace((0.354, 0.54),(0, 0.63397459621)), black+0.4bp); draw(brace((0.649, 0.456),(0.354, 0.54)), black+0.4bp); draw(arc((r, 0), r, 0, 180)); draw(arc((1, r), r, 90, 270)); draw(arc((1 - r, 1), r, 180, 360)); draw(arc((0, 1 - r), r, 270, 450)); draw(circle((1/2,1/2),R)); label(&quot;$r$&quot;, (0.81, 0.338)); label(&quot;$r$&quot;, (0.164, 0.515)); label(&quot;$d_{1}$&quot;, (0.49, 0.42)); [/asy]\" width=\"285\" height=\"285\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/c/cac04fa2c971377a4bafe873c5b7be5cd867d0eb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2r+d_{1} = d+d_{1}\\]\" width=\"127\" height=\"15\" />\nTherefore, we equate them, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/8/278fbb902690dfaa209c93bbb7a7abb86d5a2cbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, and substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/7/407e37ac3b0f77749ed2764493e32e5a710e4a08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d= \\sqrt{3}-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/a/6aa6ae95f27490d28a2e4348e6559521df2eaa3c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d+d_{1} = d\\sqrt{2}\\]\" width=\"106\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/e/fbeb521996f76487819c884794486c32e496023c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d_{1} = d\\sqrt{2} - d\\]\" width=\"106\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc637d3d92b3e28b327f64f387440691df99092c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d_{1} = d(\\sqrt{2} - 1)\\]\" width=\"118\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/f/cff36988aabbebe2009ca1d72c701d6033534875.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d_{1} = (\\sqrt{2}-1)(\\sqrt{3}-1)\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"21\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/a/97a4a31cf6c65ffe9eba04cf0c187643ead61cb1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2+3-2 = 3 \\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 3}\\]\" width=\"210\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~shockfront99\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_.28Logical.2C_Good_Editing.2C_.7E0:40.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:40)\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:40)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:40)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/S1mFur6p64U\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/S1mFur6p64U</a>\n</p><p>~Ebai\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.28Quick_and_Simple.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(Quick_and_Simple)\">Video Solution(Quick and Simple)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(Quick and Simple)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2BVdHsX9dtg\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2BVdHsX9dtg</a>\n~Sigma_Bob\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dLSWVrrKsgs\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dLSWVrrKsgs</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_OmegaLearn.org\">Video Solution 2 by OmegaLearn.org</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by OmegaLearn.org\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ttjGbBlkBfI\">https://youtu.be/ttjGbBlkBfI</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_3_.28Fast_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3_(Fast_and_Easy)\">Video Solution 3 (Fast and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3 (Fast and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e6Yyk8C_TQc\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e6Yyk8C_TQc</a>\n</p><p>~ Pi Academy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_4_by_MadMath\">Video Solution 4 by MadMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 4 by MadMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/GCJbqdHEAk4\">https://youtu.be/GCJbqdHEAk4</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; w